    "body": "@hsivonen Also I tried to use this code with some parsers (for example https://astexplorer.net/) and most of them parse them as comments (i.e. like google/safari/edge).\r\n\r\n> AFAICT, the Firefox behavior is correct both in terms of the intent of the design (copypaste from XML-based SVG working)\r\n\r\nCan you clarify?\r\n\r\n> in terms of the spec language (the adjusted current node indeed is in the SVG namespace, which is not the HTML namespace).\r\n\r\nBut we have [HTML integration point](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#html-integration-point), what in fact in the name means what we will have HTML inside, so `CDATA` in HTML context is bogus comment\r\n\r\nI'm not trying to argue, I just want to clarify the logic, because many different instruments behave differently",
