    "updated_at": "2022-11-29T19:31:14Z",
    "body": "> @hsivonen Also I tried to use this code with some parsers (for example https://astexplorer.net/) and most of them parse them as comments (i.e. like google/safari/edge).\r\n> \r\n> > AFAICT, the Firefox behavior is correct both in terms of the intent of the design (copypaste from XML-based SVG working)\r\n> \r\n> Can you clarify?\r\n\r\nThe reason why the CDATA stuff exists in the first place is to support copying and pasting SVG source from an XML-based .svg file inline into HTML. Since SVG `title`, etc., can contain a text node in SVG and text nodes in SVG can be serialized as CDATA sections, it makes sense to support CDATA sections in that context.\r\n\r\nOTOH, for nested HTML, we prioritize HTMLness over an SVG ancestor.\r\n\r\n> > in terms of the spec language (the adjusted current node indeed is in the SVG namespace, which is not the HTML namespace).\r\n> \r\n> But we have [HTML integration point](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#html-integration-point), what in fact in the name means what we will have HTML inside, so `CDATA` in HTML context is bogus comment\r\n\r\nYou can't infer that from the name. The key thing is what you quoted from https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#markup-declaration-open-state in your original report.\r\n\r\n> Even more (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#tree-construction):\r\n> \r\n> > If the [adjusted current node](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#adjusted-current-node) is an element in the [HTML namespace](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#html-namespace)\r\n> > ...\r\n> > If the [adjusted current node](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#adjusted-current-node) is an [HTML integration point](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#html-integration-point) and the token is a start tag\r\n> > If the [adjusted current node](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#adjusted-current-node) is an [HTML integration point](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#html-integration-point) and the token is a character token\r\n> > If the token is an end-of-file token\r\n> > Process the token according to the rules given in the section corresponding to the current [insertion mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insertion-mode) in HTML content.\r\n> \r\n> So any element in the HTML namespace and `adjusted current node is an HTML integration point and the token is a character token` parsed as\r\n> \r\n> > Process the token according to the rules given in the section corresponding to the current [insertion mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insertion-mode) in HTML content.\r\n\r\nBy the time we get to tree construction, the tokenizer has already resolved the CDATA section either into character tokens or into a comment token. There's no contradiction.\r\n\r\nI think the spec is already pretty clear. Yet, there's an implementation bug (singular; inherited from WebKit into Blink). We need html5lib-tests / WPT coverage for this more than we need spec clarification.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
