    "body": "@hsivonen \r\n\r\n> The reason why the CDATA stuff exists in the first place is to support copying and pasting SVG source from an XML-based .svg file inline into HTML. Since SVG title, etc., can contain a text node in SVG and text nodes in SVG can be serialized as CDATA sections, it makes sense to support CDATA sections in that context.\r\n\r\n> OTOH, for nested HTML, we prioritize HTMLness over an SVG ancestor.\r\n\r\nSounds reasonable for me :+1: \r\n\r\nThank you for the answer, I will add test cases in `html5lib-tests` in future",
